  data:  # 7b72
    kind: work_item  # 7b72
    title: "auto-pr --detach: background its own CI poll and return a resumable handle (WI-katap ergonomics half)"  # 7b72
    status: todo_hard  # 7b72
    priority: 2  # 7b72
    parent:  # 7b72
    tags:  # 7b72
    - ci_infrastructure  # 7b72
    isbefore: []  # 7b72
    duplicate_of: []  # 7b72
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 7b72
    pr_ref:  # 7b72
    description: "auto-pr's blocking CI poll does not fit an agent harness's foreground budget, and no amount of tuning makes it fit: the poll defaults to 2400s, the 300s soft-retry is not optional, and a foreground shell call is capped at 600s (Claude Code). WI-katap made the resulting kill VISIBLE (it now records terminated_sigterm rather than INV-rahib's `unknown` violation signal) but did nothing about the ergonomics: the run still dies with the merge unfinished, and a human or agent still completes it by hand with `merge-pr <N> --wait-for-ci`. Measured: 22 of 84 post-instrumentation runs, 14 of the 15 PRs behind them merged anyway.\n\nThe workaround that already works is `nohup ./scripts/auto-pr > log 2>&1 &`, now written into AGENTS.md. It is a workaround because the caller has to know to do it, has to invent a log path, and gets no declared state from the parent -- the prior session rediscovered it and then reverted to `timeout 590` within the SAME session.\n\nPROPOSED SHAPE (owner said \"scope it in now\" on 2026-09-20; design not yet reviewed):\n  * `auto-pr --detach` does the bounded work in the foreground -- push, PR create/find -- then re-execs itself as a detached watcher (setsid + nohup, stdio to a standard log path), writes a handle, records a DECLARED terminal state for the parent, and returns 0 immediately.\n  * The detached child runs the poll + merge and appends its OWN ledger row, so one logical PR yields two honest rows rather than one lie.\n  * `auto-pr wait [--timeout N]` blocks in CALLER-SIZED chunks against the handle, so an agent can check in within its budget and resume next turn.\n  * The handle, not an ad-hoc /tmp path, is the discovery mechanism; PR_PENDING remains the gate.\n\nOPEN QUESTIONS for review, not yet decided:\n  1. Does `--detach` become the DEFAULT for non-tty callers? Tempting and risky -- it changes the contract of the script that merges every PR.\n  2. What terminal state does the parent record? It did not merge and did not fail; it handed off. Probably a new deliberate-non-merge value, which needs the same both-directions vocabulary treatment WI-katap's fourth bucket got.\n  3. What happens when a detached watcher is itself killed (machine sleep, session teardown)? The handle must distinguish \"still watching\" from \"watcher died mid-poll\", or this re-creates the absent-vs-empty defect one level out."  # 7b72
    fields: {}  # 7b72
